EXL3 is Turboderp's trellis quantization format and tooling. This fork reads
EXL3 checkpoints and decodes the format on Metal; it does not include
ExLlamaV3's quantizer. The EXL3 checkpoints used for development and
measurement were quantized by Turboderp and are distributed under the
licenses of their respective base models.

QTIP
----
Trellis-coded quantization originates in the QTIP research line
("QTIP: Quantization with Trellises and Incoherence Processing",
Tseng et al.). The EXL3 format builds on that work.

trellis-serve
-------------
The bit-exact EXL3 reference implementation vendored in conversion/exl3.py
derives from the trellis-serve reference. It is included for conversion
correctness and retains its original attribution in the file header.

